MID_LGV_2_M03_Bel_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Bel_m01_001: At one point, I served Arago's king as a general.\nNow I return as an invader.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Bel_m01_002: But what else is there to do? This is how we create a\njust world.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Bel_m01: <BLN>It's the only path.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Seo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Seo_m01_001: A difficult march and an offensive with a small force.\nYet no part of me feels we are at risk of defeat.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Seo_m01_002: I suspect this is because redoubtable warriors have\nrallied to my side.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Seo_m01_003: It may be the connections we forged during the\nHeroic Games. Or perhaps...
MID_LGA_2_M03_Seo_m01: <BLN>They are staunch allies.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Tia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Tia_m01_001: I got a letter from my grandpa. At first, I thought he\nwas checking in to see how I'm doing...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Tia_m01_002: What he'd actually written me was a detailed method\nfor grasping enemy movement and escape routes.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Tia_m01_003: I'll admit, it is clear that he's sharing those ideas\nbecause he's worried about me.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Tia_m01_004: But he could have at least offered a sentence or two\nabout how he's getting on!
MID_LGA_2_M03_Tia_m01: <BLN>Oh, Grandpa!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Pet_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Pet_m01_001: My dad wasn't happy with the idea of me going to\nDagsion. I wonder how he's doing...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Pet_m01_002: I'm only still alive because he taught me how to use\na bow.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Pet_m01_003: As soon as I'm home again, I'm going to tell him\nthank you for saving my life.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Pet_m01: <BLN>Dad...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Hur_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Hur_m01_001: I keep thinking about Noah and Cezarie.\nI worry they're hungry.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Hur_m01_002: It happens every time I eat. I can see their faces, and\nI think about how they're why I'm doing this.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Hur_m01: <BLN>I worry they're hungry...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Max_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Max_m01_001: If all goes well, Grand Aragon's going to become a\nbattlefield.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Max_m01_002: How much blood gets soaked into the ground—\nthat's up to us. Heh heh!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Max_m01_003: No matter where the king goes, I follow, with a\nsmile on my face.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Max_m01: <BLN>If all goes well...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Gol_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Gol_m01_001: My tribe, the Chetaur, had some kinda dustup\nwith Brezarant.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Gol_m01_002: During the Mons Uprising, we got pulled\ninto rebelling against the king.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Gol_m01_003: Been getting a LOT of questions about that time\nfrom a certain someone. Know what I said?
MID_LGV_2_M03_Gol_m01_004: "That's old hat. What my brother and me got going—\nthat's new hat!"
MID_LGA_2_M03_Gol_m01: <BLN>Stupid questions.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Gat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Gat_m01_001: Will this plan bring us good fortune or ill? It's too\nearly to tell.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Gat_m01_002: But I see a king confident in his ideals.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Gat_m01_003: Given that, I will make no objections, but merely\ngather soldiers and charge into battle.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Gat_m01: <BLN>Good or ill?
MID_LGV_2_M03_Dan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Dan_m01_001: A magnificent story unfolds! A king crossing the\nultimate threshold, and now charging forth.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Dan_m01_002: Trodding again in the land where he was born and\nraised, toward the woman he loves.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Dan_m01_003: A country ruled by his former friend—now his most\nhated adversary. What awaits? We shall see!
MID_LGA_2_M03_Dan_m01: <BLN>How will it end?!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Fab_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Fab_m01_001: King Gilchris seems to be quite notorious, and yet it\nappears that the throne remains in his grasp.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Fab_m01_002: Beast or no, it is only natural that a leader unfit for\nthe role be ousted.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Fab_m01_003: Yet it is not so. Either his land is rife with cowardice,\nor the children of the goddess prop him up.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Fab_m01: <BLN>King Gilchris...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Esm_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Esm_m01_001: As the war drags on, the fighting is getting more and\nmore intense.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Esm_m01_002: I don't enjoy it the way Sweetie does.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Esm_m01_003: The Heroic Games made sense to me, because it was\nall to get your wish granted.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Esm_m01: <BLN>I don't enjoy fighting.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Urs_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Urs_m01_001: I've always loved flowers that bloom in the shade...\nFlowers that bloom quietly, unnoticed.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Urs_m01_002: They may go unloved, but they're happy for their\nentire lives up until the end.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Urs_m01_003: We're similar in that way. I... I don't need to be\nloved...to live.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Urs_m01: <BLN>I don't need to be loved...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sim_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sim_m01_001: Honestly, I still can't believe it.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sim_m01_002: First, Emperor Dagda turns into a dragon and attacks\nus, then the stars start falling out of the sky!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sim_m01_003: Hard to believe I'm even breathing right now.\nEven more reason to see this through.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Sim_m01: <BLN>I still can't believe it.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Lou_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Lou_m01_001: I never expected anything like this! First, a dragon\nattacks us, then a star falls right on him!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Lou_m01_002: If I wasn't busy fighting for my life, I might just write\nthis into a new story!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Lou_m01_003: But if I want to write anything ever again, I have to\nmake sure I don't die first!
MID_LGA_2_M03_Lou_m01: <BLN>Don't die, no matter what!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Fia_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Fia_m01_001: The Divine Emperor turned into a dragon and killed\nso many...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Fia_m01_002: It seems he truly intends to wipe us all out...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Fia_m01_003: If that's the case, then fine. I'll use my strength\nto help end him.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Fia_m01: <BLN>I've made up my mind.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Die_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Die_m01_001: Whatever the plan is, I'll be sure to follow it.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Die_m01_002: I wonder if we'll meet again after this battle,\nOrchel...
MID_LGA_2_M03_Die_m01: <BLN>After this battle...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Lor_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Lor_m01_001: They say King Gilchris of Arago shows no mercy\nto those who stand up to him.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Lor_m01_002: But we've crossed the desert to fight him.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Lor_m01_003: It's going to be tough, but I'm ready for what's\nnext. There's no way I'll give up now!
MID_LGA_2_M03_Lor_m01: <BLN>King Gilchris...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Set_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Set_m01_001: No matter the era, war is a terrible thing. Blood\nflows, tears gush, and the weak are first to die.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Set_m01_002: That's why I'm determined to put an end to this war.\nA bold ambition for a mere traveler, I suppose.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Set_m01: <BLN>Damnable war...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Nin_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Nin_m01_001: Hmm... Javelins of light... Is that something the\nhumans made? It's not like any of Credna's Arcs.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Nin_m01_002: I sensed it was not a weapon in spirit, however...\nmore an entity that hungered for destruction.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Nin_m01: <BLN>Javelins of light...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Bon_m01_001: How frustrating... I am Her Majesty's tactician,\nyet it is Bertrand who devised our stratagem.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Bon_m01_004: I had never considered a route that bypasses\nArago's main force entirely.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Bon_m01_002: But his outlandish scheme does have a certain\nappeal. A means of bypassing Arago's main force...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Bon_m01_005: But Bertrand's outlandish scheme does have a certain\nappeal, even to an orthodox tactician like me.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Bon_m01_003: And since Your Majesty agrees, I must draw up plans\nat once for urban warfare!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Bon_m01_006: I must make up for it by devising my own\nimprovements to the plan as we go.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Bon_m01: <BLN>Such a daring stratagem!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Tob_m01_001: Baw haw haw! We're gonna take on Arago with our\nthree thousand soldiers!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Tob_m01_002: I'm itchin' to get started. A true warrior can pull off\ngreat feats even when outnumbered!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Tob_m01_003: Now to fill our bellies and get ready to cross\nthe desert!
MID_LGA_2_M03_Tob_m01: <BLN>We're gonna fight Arago!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Lil_m01_001: Another tough-to-pull-off plan... Coming from the\nforests of Saramis, the desert heat sure is rough.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Lil_m01_002: But if they say this is the most effective way to win,\nthen I can't complain.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Lil_m01_003: I'll do it for the big payday I've got coming...plus for\nthe sake of my family back in Saramis.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Lil_m01: <BLN>The dry desert heat sure is rough.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Lys_m01_001: I wonder if we ought to hold a feast as a way for\nSaramis and Brezarant soldiers to mingle.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Lys_m01_002: A training session with a meal should be enough,\nright? I don't think we'd need to provide liquor.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Lys_m01_003: Though I'm not one to talk, seeing as I don't drink\nmuch. Still...
MID_LGA_2_M03_Lys_m01: <BLN>Should we hold a feast?
MID_LGV_2_M03_Buc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Buc_m01_001: As we go forward, I can't help but remember that the\nkingdom of Arago once attacked Cydonia.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Buc_m01_003: As we go forward, I can't help but remember that the\nkingdom of Arago once attacked Cydonia.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Buc_m01_002: Whatever milady's intentions, I have to keep you\nfrom harm. In that there can be no doubt.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Buc_m01_004: But worry not. My blade will not be dulled or\nshaken by my emotions.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Buc_m01: <BLN>It occurs to me...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sci_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sci_m01_001: I have not set foot in the kingdom of Arago since\nthat fateful day.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sci_m01_002: The breathtaking dancing in that tavern... It feels like\na distant memory now.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Sci_m01: <BLN>Not since that fateful day.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Moo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Moo_m01_001: So, we're going through the desert to Grand Aragon?\nI don't know much about tactics, but it seems risky.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Moo_m01_002: Though...I guess there are some things you have to\ndo despite the risk.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Moo_m01_003: Anyway, I'm volunteering for the attack. I don't like\nto sit things out. Guess I get that from Mom.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Moo_m01: <BLN>We'll cross the desert.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Mic_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Mic_m01_001: I caught wind of a plan—Saramis is defending Fort\nZanbar using old folks and children.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Mic_m01_002: I won't lie to you. When I heard that, my first instinct\nwas to punch Queen Theodora in the face.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Mic_m01_005: I won't lie to you. When I heard that, I couldn't help\nbut be angry.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Mic_m01_003: But the soldiers are on board with the plan. It's their\nfamilies, after all, so it's moving forward.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Mic_m01_004: Me? I'll stretch myself to the limit so we can win and\nthey can all be reunited.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Mic_m01: <BLN>Let's win this thing.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Oly_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Oly_m01_001: The scars left by the Divine Emperor are so deep.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Oly_m01_002: The number of soldiers whom, in mere moments,\nthat god reduced to bone!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Oly_m01_003: Kalla's father he may be, but I cannot abide such\nwanton cruelty.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Oly_m01: <BLN>The brutality!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Naz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Naz_m01_001: I swear, I knew it as soon as I saw that dragon...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Naz_m01_002: I knew that's the one that burned my hometown\nway back when.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Naz_m01_003: We can't let up. We gotta keep going until the end.\nHe's not dead yet.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Naz_m01: <BLN>I knew it...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sar_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sar_m01_001: How could our ancestors create a weapon\nlike Artemis?
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sar_m01_002: 
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sar_m01_005: Such a thing shouldn't be trusted to anyone.\nPeople rarely use such power responsibly.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sar_m01_003: 
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sar_m01_006: But I trust Anatolia will know the right time to use it.\nAnd when not to.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sar_m01_004: 
MID_LGA_2_M03_Sar_m01: <BLN>Artemis...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Dai_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Dai_m01_001: Dagda! That guy's a total monster! He bulked up like\nthat in the middle of a war!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Dai_m01_002: He must just be sitting around eating and drinking\nwhile everyone else is fighting!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Dai_m01_003: I knew he was bad, but now I see he's really bad!
MID_LGA_2_M03_Dai_m01: <BLN>That total monster!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Hal_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Hal_m01_001: Traveling, sleeping, and eating with so many people\nreminds me of Nasshim's Circus.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Hal_m01_002: There's still a lot that makes me anxious, but I do\nenjoy marching with everyone else.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Hal_m01_003: I wonder if people would maybe think that was\ninsensitive to say?
MID_LGA_2_M03_Hal_m01: <BLN>Insensitive? Maybe.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Guj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Guj_m01_001: I could sing odes about this stuff all day long!\nI haven't had this much fun in ages!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Guj_m01_002: A dragon shows up! A star plummets to earth!\nWhat's next? Will the ocean flip over?
MID_LGV_2_M03_Guj_m01_003: This war is getting really interesting! I'll never\nget bored at this rate.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Guj_m01: <BLN>It's so great!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Yan_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Yan_m01_001: When Dagda was struck by that "star," how thrilling\nit was to see him turn tail and flutter away!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Yan_m01_002: Now that was a mighty power if ever I saw one.\nFolks in the city likely thought it a natural disaster.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Yan_m01_003: But even my ancestors who possessed such a\ngreat power were destroyed. How fleeting life is!
MID_LGA_2_M03_Yan_m01: <BLN>Such a mighty power!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Iio_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Iio_m01_001: I never thought I'd return to Arago in this way. Now,\njust what is happening here...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Iio_m01_002: Forgive me, Father... I suspect I won't be able to\nvisit your grave this year.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Iio_m01_003: And Mother... I hope you are safe, wherever you\nare now. I can only wish for your welfare now.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Iio_m01: <BLN>Coming home this way...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Pep_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Pep_m01_001: A ruler must take a path that's far from safe\nor unsullied.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Pep_m01_002: We are aware that a ruler must often lead the\nmarch—coated in blood, wreathed in grit!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Pep_m01_003: We have no intention of doing anything less than the\nrulers of Brezarant and Saramis in this desert!
MID_LGA_2_M03_Pep_m01: <BLN>Into the thick of it!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Noc_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Noc_m01_001: Now that I think of it, maybe someone from my\ntribe is in the Brezarant army.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Noc_m01_002: There are lots of them who love fighting. I bet\nthey'd gladly volunteer.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Noc_m01_003: I don't want to meet up with them though, so I\nhope they're not mixed in with those soldiers.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Noc_m01: <BLN>Now that I think of it...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sop_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sop_m01_001: It seems that some people will exploit others\nduring war. I should be careful!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sop_m01_002: I mean, blackmail and extortion... I could certainly\nhandle those if I had to but...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Sop_m01_003: No, if someone's going to come for me, I hope it's a\ngood ol' fashioned mugging! Much less of a hassle.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Sop_m01: <BLN>I should be careful!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Cat_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Cat_m01_001: {SetColor=Gray}Hmm...I still can't believe that Queen Theodora\nput a stop to all of the looting...{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGV_2_M03_Cat_m01_002: {SetColor=Gray}How Bertrand was able to work out a solution with\nHer Majesty... This is all almost beyond belief...{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGV_2_M03_Cat_m01_003: {SetColor=Gray}It's made...a lasting impression on me that the queen\ndid so while fearing for the survival of her nation...{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGV_2_M03_Cat_m01_004: Oh my! Queen Theodora! Y-you didn't happen to\nhear me musing aloud, did you?
MID_LGA_2_M03_Cat_m01: <BLN>How surprising...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Ned_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Ned_m01_001: {SetColor=Gray}A warrior's skill can be worth much, little, or nothing\nat all... In sum, that value is based on battle tactics...{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGV_2_M03_Ned_m01_002: {SetColor=Gray}And while King Bertrand's leadership is masterful...\nI hope his strategy will now lead the way...{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGA_2_M03_Ned_m01: <BLN>King Bertrand's strategy...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Zac_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Zac_m01_001: There was a knight around here sharing his\ngrub with kids. Unbelievable!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Zac_m01_002: Hmm... But maybe that knight was really tryin'\nto get paid back five times over!
MID_LGA_2_M03_Zac_m01: <BLN>Unbelievable!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Maj_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Maj_m01_001: {SetColor=Gray}Still can't believe that Bertrand guy became king\nof Brezarant...{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGV_2_M03_Maj_m01_002: {SetColor=Gray}Still remember the first time I saw the guy... Long\ntime ago too... Tried to make him lick my feet...{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGV_2_M03_Maj_m01_003: {SetColor=Gray}Damn shame... If things had gone my way, I'd be\nfamous for gettin' a king to grovel...{SetColor=Default}
MID_LGA_2_M03_Maj_m01: <BLN>I screwed that up...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Ven_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Ven_m01_001: Being at war reminds me of my early days as a\nsoldier. My superiors really bullied me!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Ven_m01_002: They'd throw mud in my food and make me eat it,\nor else they'd make my training way worse!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Ven_m01_003: I know one must suffer hardship to rise to the\noccasion...but I never got a taste for dirt.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Ven_m01: <BLN>Back in my early days...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Ini_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Ini_m01_001: Good time for mercenaries to make a profit, but\nstill, I wish this war would end soon.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Ini_m01_002: I hate watching anyone die, even my worst\nenemies.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Ini_m01_003: Faces twisted in pain... Voices wailing in horror...\nUgh, I miss more peaceful times.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Ini_m01: <BLN>I miss how things were...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Jas_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Jas_m01_001: I saved up a little bit of money so far. But I need\nto keep on making more, bit by bit.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Jas_m01_002: The longer the war goes on, the more I could make.\nWhen peace returns, I might make very little.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Jas_m01_003: I hope this all ends well. But I doubt it will.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Jas_m01: <BLN>It's been good so far.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Ale_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Ale_m01_001: Bucephalus used to get quite ornery if he didn't\neat enough. But he's been well-behaved lately.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Ale_m01_002: It's like he knows that I, and everyone else, are\nstruggling with this whole, desperate situation.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Ale_m01_003: But I'd like for this all to end soon. I'd like for him\nto eat his fill.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Ale_m01: <BLN>He's a good boy...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Cen_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Cen_m01_001: Were I not a vulkan in Aurora's temple, I would\nmost likely be fighting as part of the empire.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Cen_m01_002: Obeying the divine command would involve either\nrazing Saramis or dying on the battlefield.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Cen_m01_003: Aurora saved me from walking that path of suffering.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Cen_m01: <BLN>If things had been different...
MID_LGV_2_M03_Kir_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Kir_m01_001: I'd done my fair share of taking advantage of war.\nI used to attack merchant ships in the chaos.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Kir_m01_002: I'd love to steal a ship and get back to it...if I\ndidn't keep seeing the ghosts of those I've killed.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Kir_m01_003: But no ship could compare to that beauty I used to\ncaptain. Ah, that poor ship...
MID_LGA_2_M03_Kir_m01: <BLN>Always take advantage!
MID_LGV_2_M03_Nuz_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Nuz_m01_001: If the queen of Saramis says we will cross the desert,\nthen the Har Hali warriors will not shrink from it.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Nuz_m01_002: The forest peoples are accustomed to living off the\nland. We will rise to this occasion.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Nuz_m01: <BLN>We will do as the queen says.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Hri_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Hri_m01_001: Here I am! A traitor to my homeland, living here\nin disgrace.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Hri_m01_002: And now I am readying to join an attack on my\ncountry of origin.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Hri_m01_003: Then again, maybe... Maybe this is what I was\nmeant to do all along.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Hri_m01: <BLN>Imagine it.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Tro_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_Tro_m01_001: That little stunt tired me out.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Tro_m01_002: Controlling a star requires more concentration than\nyou can probably imagine.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Tro_m01_003: If I let my focus slip even a little, it could have ended\nup raining down on our own heads.
MID_LGV_2_M03_Tro_m01_004: Just between you and me, I'm relieved I managed it.
MID_LGA_2_M03_Tro_m01: <BLN>That stunt tired me out.
MID_LGV_2_M03_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_B01_m01_001: My elderly mother headed to Fort Zanbar to help\ndefend it. But she's never fought a day in her life!
MID_LGV_2_M03_B01_m01_002: She said she couldn't do nothing with her country,\nher family, and her beloved queen on the line.
MID_LGV_2_M03_B01_m01_003: I'm proud to have a mother like her. I'll do my best\nso she can be proud of me too!
MID_LGA_2_M03_B01_m01: <BLN>I'll do her proud!
MID_LGV_2_M03_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_B02_m01_001: I guess deserts are kind of like a sea of sand. But I'll\nstill miss the sound of the waves.
MID_LGV_2_M03_B02_m01_002: Whether it's fighting or fishing, the sea is where\nI'm in my element. Too bad this isn't a naval war.
MID_LGA_2_M03_B02_m01: <BLN>The desert, huh?
MID_LGV_2_M03_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_B03_m01_001: I wonder if that child I left behind is OK...she had\njust turned 10 years old.
MID_LGV_2_M03_B03_m01_002: She was saying stuff like "I want to fight, just like\nmy mom!" I wish I could at least get a letter to her.
MID_LGV_2_M03_B03_m01_003: But wishing for the impossible gets you nowhere.\nI've just got to return to her as soon as I can...
MID_LGA_2_M03_B03_m01: <BLN>I want to get back to her soon...
MID_LGV_2_M03_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_B04_m01_001: Over mountains, valleys, rivers, and even the desert!
MID_LGV_2_M03_B04_m01_002: The noble blood of the Asherah flows in my veins.\nI'll march on tirelessly to our destination!
MID_LGA_2_M03_B04_m01: <BLN>I'll go anywhere!
MID_LGV_2_M03_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_B05_m01_001: Her Majesty doesn't have a bloodmark but can\nmatch the king in strength.
MID_LGV_2_M03_B05_m01_002: If things had gone differently between our nations,\nI wonder how the fight would have gone.
MID_LGA_2_M03_B05_m01: <BLN>I wonder who would have won...
MID_LGV_2_M03_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_2_M03_B06_m01_001: I'm not sure when it happened, but I've gotten used\nto fighting side by side with the Saraminians.
MID_LGV_2_M03_B06_m01_002: I was nervous they'd be a spooky crowd with weird\nbeliefs, but not really. They're pretty good folks.
MID_LGA_2_M03_B06_m01: <BLN>You get used to it.